@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Approve the exact reviewed envelope
+
+The daemon IPC method `approve_reviewed` accepts one `entry_id` and an
+`expected_envelope_digest` in `sha256:` plus 64 hexadecimal digits format.
+Use the exact digest returned with the reviewed preview. Existing approval
+scope, expiry, policy and upload checks still apply.
+
+The daemon checks the stored preview digest and Pending state under the same
+queue lock that approves the entry. A stale/missing pin returns
+`reviewed-envelope-changed`; the operation never implicitly builds a preview.
+Bulk selectors (`all`, `project_id`, `filter`) and content/outcome mutations
+(`correction`, `outcome`) are rejected, even when supplied as false or null.
+Missing/malformed required fields return `exact-review-parameters-required`.
+Other existing entry, policy and persistence failures retain their own labels.
+
+The ordinary `approve` method retains its existing semantics. A distinct method
+name makes an older daemon reject the new call rather than ignore a new field on
+`approve`. Clients must not fall back to ordinary approval after rejection.
+This is approval, not an upload receipt. A lost response is an uncertain outcome,
+not permission to retry automatically. This method alone adds no persistent
+revocation fence or recovery endpoint.
